Subject: Validate source map content before automapping on non-Node targets

Source map URLs and contents can be controlled by the inspected page. Automapping previously bypassed content validation for all source-map-derived resources regardless of the target type.

This change ensures that content validation is enforced for source map UISourceCodes on non-Node targets, preventing unintended bindings to local files when contents do not match. Unvalidated source map bindings are now restricted to Node.js targets.

Bug: 528485835
Change-Id: I352227d1a43b1e6cc9209eede6500c9d5d59d7eb
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8511659
Reviewed-by: Jack Franklin <jacktfranklin@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
front_end/models/persistence/Automapping.test.ts does not exist on this branch; the test-only hunk for that file was dropped. The Automapping.ts change applied unchanged.

